WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.255 --> 00:00:04.550
Ladies and gentlemen, in my short stay,

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.410
Chicago has been very nice to me.

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:08.210
And of course Chicago's a drinking town,

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:10.220
and earlier this week,
(audience cheering)

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:12.520
earlier this week the Goose Island Brewery

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:15.850
announced they were creating
(audience cheering)

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:17.910
a special ale in my honor.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.410
I decided to pay them a visit

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:23.536
and learn how you make
a Conan O'Brien brew.

00:00:23.536 --> 00:00:24.471
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:24.471 --> 00:00:29.471
♪ Beer, we like to drink beer ♪

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.273
♪ Beer, we like to drink our beer ♪

00:00:33.273 --> 00:00:35.030
This is Greg Hall.
Right.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:37.150
You are the brewmaster
here at Goose Island.

00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:37.983
True.

00:00:37.983 --> 00:00:40.130
Is brewmaster an official title?

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:41.730
Do you need a certificate?

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.270
Actually it's master brewer
is kind of the official one.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:47.160
What do you prefer, master
brewer or brewmaster?

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.750
I think the brewmaster sounds--

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:51.460
You gotta admit, it just sounds great.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:53.920
Yeah.
Behold, brewmaster.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.413
Yes.
(audience laughing)

00:00:55.413 --> 00:00:56.576
♪ Beer ♪
Come with me.

00:00:56.576 --> 00:01:00.097
♪ Beer, oh, beer ♪

00:01:00.097 --> 00:01:02.866
Whoa! (screams)

00:01:02.866 --> 00:01:05.190
We got Will, Will is the
head brewer of our brewpub.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.023
Hey, Will.
Hello.

00:01:06.023 --> 00:01:09.020
We have Ryan, his able-bodied assistant.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.130
The term is called Brewpies.
Brewpies.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:14.770
The women that stand up in
the window and watch us brew.

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:16.155
Right.
They're Brewpies.

00:01:16.155 --> 00:01:16.988
Brewpies.

00:01:16.988 --> 00:01:18.508
They try to get with the brewers.

00:01:18.508 --> 00:01:22.627
(audience laughing)
♪ Oh yeah, drink my beer ♪

00:01:22.627 --> 00:01:25.627
(audience cheering)

00:01:28.963 --> 00:01:30.442
Oh!

00:01:30.442 --> 00:01:32.870
♪ Open beer ♪

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:34.593
(audience laughing)

00:01:34.593 --> 00:01:36.960
(grunting) Son of a bitch!

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:40.265
Laughed at me, laughed at my naked body!

00:01:40.265 --> 00:01:43.657
Do you also wear protective
glasses, why is that?

00:01:43.657 --> 00:01:47.533
Hey look, I got my beer
goggles on. (laughs)

00:01:48.532 --> 00:01:50.170
Did you hear what I said?
Beer goggles.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:51.850
Yeah.
(audience laughing)

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:55.410
What we thought was we would
make a kind of a red ale.

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:58.770
Conan Red, tell me about the
ingredients of Conan's beer.

00:01:58.770 --> 00:01:59.950
Well, we're gonna use some...

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:02.040
And refer to it as Conan's
beer in the third person.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:03.500
When we're making Conan's beer--

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.760
Mm-hmm, is that Conan
O'Brien the talk show host?

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.030
Yeah.
That guy's funny.

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:08.470
Funny guy.

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:10.133
If it's a Conan beer it
should have a big head on it,

00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:11.610
you know what I'm saying?
It should have a big head.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:12.443
We can do that.
Is that a funny--

00:02:12.443 --> 00:02:13.276
We can manage that.

00:02:13.276 --> 00:02:14.830
I have high, sharp cheekbones.

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.680
What could capture that in a beer?

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.110
Could be the glass we serve it in.

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:20.180
Very nice.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.941
I have a very thin,
almost nonexistent ass.

00:02:22.941 --> 00:02:24.210
(audience laughing)
What would you do?

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:27.440
Stemware.
Stemware, nice, I like it.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:31.740
Here's my pitch, all the world
knows that I'm very pale.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:33.070
This is a shirtless photo of me

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:36.313
taken after a week in the sun.
A week.

00:02:36.313 --> 00:02:39.670
Conan's pale, that's why
I pitch to you right now,

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:43.960
Conan O'Brien Pale Ale.
(audience laughs and cheers)

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.570
And we'd offer, for people who want it,

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:49.600
a Conan O'Brien Pale, Pale Ale.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:50.478
(audience laughing)
Is that a good plan?

00:02:50.478 --> 00:02:51.341
[Greg] I think it's a good idea.

00:02:51.341 --> 00:02:55.410
♪ Beer, beer, we like to drink our beer ♪

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:56.246
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:02:56.246 --> 00:02:59.313
♪ Beer beer, we like to drink our beer ♪

00:02:59.313 --> 00:03:03.070
♪ Beer, beer, drink our beer ♪

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:07.225
Well, I think we...
(audience cheers and claps)

00:03:07.225 --> 00:03:12.225
I think we should have an expert
test the Conan O'Brien Ale

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.130
so here to do that, once
again, George Wendt.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:18.710
Let's get him out here.
(crowd applauds and cheers)

00:03:22.721 --> 00:03:24.956
Thank you, Conan.
Yeah, there you go.

00:03:24.956 --> 00:03:27.977
(crowd cheering and clapping)

00:03:27.977 --> 00:03:30.766
[Crowd] Chug, chug, chug,
chug, chug, chug, chug, chug!

00:03:30.766 --> 00:03:33.599
(Chewbacca roars)

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:39.520
(crowd cheering)

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:43.390
I guess that means it's good.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:44.269
We'll be right back.

00:03:44.269 --> 00:03:45.852
Wilco will be here!

